  "text": "Classic Neapolitan ice cream is a trio of three contrasting flavors: vanilla, chocolate, and strawberry. Since it's a traditional Italian dessert, it's often enjoyed in a cone or served in a dish with the three scoops side by side.\n\nHere's a simple recipe for **homemade Neapolitan ice cream**:\n\n---\n\n### \ud83c\udf66 Classic Neapolitan Ice Cream Recipe\n\n**Ingredients** (makes one batch, about 4\u20136 servings):\n\n#### Vanilla Ice Cream:\n- 2 cups whole milk\n- 1 cup heavy cream\n- 3/4 cup sugar\n- 1 teaspoon vanilla extract\n- 1/2 tsp salt\n- 1/2 cup cornstarch (or cornflour)\n\n#### Chocolate Ice Cream:\n- 2 cups whole milk\n- 1 cup heavy cream\n- 3/4 cup sugar\n- 1/2 cup cocoa powder\n- 1/2 tsp salt\n- 1/2 cup cornstarch\n- 1/2 tsp vanilla extract\n\n#### Strawberry Ice Cream:\n- 2 cups whole milk\n- 1 cup heavy cream\n- 3/4 cup sugar\n- 1/2 cup chopped strawberries (fresh or frozen)\n- 1/2 tsp salt\n- 1/2 cup cornstarch\n- 1/2 tsp vanilla extract\n\n---\n\n### \ud83c\udf68 Instructions:\n\n1. **Prepare the Base:**\n   - In a medium saucepan, whisk together the milk, cream, sugar, salt, and cornstarch for each flavor.\n   - Cook over medium heat, stirring constantly, until the mixture thickens and reaches 170\u00b0F (77\u00b0C). This is called a \"custard base.\"\n   - Remove from heat, and stir in the vanilla extract and cocoa powder (for chocolate) or strawberries (for strawberry).\n   - Let the mixture cool to room temperature, then chill in the refrigerator for at least 4 hours or overnight.\n\n2. **Churn:**\n   - Churn each flavor in an ice cream maker according to the manufacturer\u2019s instructions, until it reaches a soft-serve consistency.\n   - If you don\u2019t have an ice cream maker, you can churn the mixture in a freezer-safe container, stirring every 30 minutes for 2\u20133 hours.\n\n3. **Freeze:**\n   - Transfer the churned ice cream to airtight containers and freeze for at least 2\u20133 hours until firm.\n\n4. **Serve:**\n   - Scoop and enjoy! For a classic touch, serve in a cone with the three flavors side by side.\n\n---\n\n### \ud83c\udf53 Tips:\n- For a richer chocolate flavor, you can use dark chocolate cocoa powder.\n- If you want a lighter chocolate, you can add a bit of melted dark chocolate to the mixture.\n- Fresh strawberries are best, but frozen strawberries will work if you stir them in while the base is still warm.\n\nEnjoy your homemade Neapolitan ice cream! \ud83c\udf68",
